1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,353
A single medicine can carry a company.

2
00:00:02,773 --> 00:00:09,221
At Takeda, Entyvio is twenty-one percent of revenue, and its exclusivity ends in the second half of this decade.

3
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:16,199
But every medicine sits inside a wider system: science, data, manufacturing, evidence, partners, patients.

4
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:20,397
So the question for the next fifteen years is not which drug comes next.

5
00:00:20,817 --> 00:00:22,528
It is what makes success repeatable.

6
00:00:26,583 --> 00:00:34,020
Eli Lilly grew from twenty-eight to sixty-five billion dollars in four years; tirzepatide became fifty-six percent of its sales.

7
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:46,332
But concentration cuts both ways: by late twenty twenty-six, realized prices had fallen fifteen percent, and one pharmacy benefit manager kept Lilly's drug off its preferred list for fifteen months.

8
00:00:46,752 --> 00:00:50,677
A single franchise creates exposure long before any patent expires.

9
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:54,360
AbbVie faced the cliff Takeda now faces.

10
00:00:54,780 --> 00:01:00,881
Humira fell from twenty-one billion dollars to four and a half billion within three years of biosimilar entry.

11
00:01:01,301 --> 00:01:07,551
Yet AbbVie recovered, because Skyrizi and Rinvoq were already on the market, across Humira's major indications.

12
00:01:07,971 --> 00:01:11,503
Contracting held ninety-seven percent of volume for over a year.

13
00:01:11,922 --> 00:01:12,936
It delayed the fall.

14
00:01:13,357 --> 00:01:14,533
It did not prevent it.

15
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:24,536
Johnson and Johnson absorbed a forty-one percent fall in Stelara with a diversified base; its largest brand is only fifteen percent of sales.

16
00:01:24,956 --> 00:01:26,480
And artificial intelligence?

17
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:35,588
Across all four companies, the research found no independent evidence that any AI programme has yet changed a cost, a timeline, or a revenue line.

18
00:01:36,008 --> 00:01:39,126
Lilly built an open robotic laboratory, then sold it.

19
00:01:39,546 --> 00:01:41,016
Announcements are not outcomes.

20
00:01:42,583 --> 00:01:43,234
Takeda.

21
00:01:43,654 --> 00:01:46,367
Entyvio brings in nine hundred fifty-eight billion yen.

22
00:01:46,787 --> 00:01:55,299
Medicare price negotiation takes effect in January twenty twenty-eight, and two biosimilar applications are already under FDA review.

23
00:01:55,718 --> 00:01:58,645
Vyvanse lost two hundred twenty billion yen in two years.

24
00:01:59,065 --> 00:02:07,555
If Entyvio erodes the way Humira did, three hundred eighty to seven hundred seventy billion yen a year is at risk; a scenario, not a forecast.

25
00:02:07,975 --> 00:02:11,731
But it defines the task: defend what is dated, and build what repeats.

26
00:02:13,283 --> 00:02:15,270
Takeda is not starting from zero.

27
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:20,447
More than two hundred seventy plasma centres, with fractionation capacity expanding.

28
00:02:20,867 --> 00:02:26,314
Its Shonan labs discovered oveporexton, approved in August twenty twenty-six for narcolepsy.

29
00:02:26,735 --> 00:02:30,233
Rusfertide followed; zasocitinib is under priority review.

30
00:02:30,653 --> 00:02:33,397
Three Phase three readouts came in positive, on plan.

31
00:02:33,817 --> 00:02:38,274
And Takeda has shown it can stop: it exited cell therapy and took the write-down.

32
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:41,401
What should Takeda build first?

33
00:02:41,821 --> 00:02:43,091
What rivals cannot buy.

34
00:02:43,512 --> 00:02:50,554
Compute can be rented and models are converging; what stays proprietary is the data a company generates when it decides.

35
00:02:50,974 --> 00:02:55,687
AbbVie connected two thousand trials into one research hub with fewer than ten staff.

36
00:02:56,107 --> 00:02:57,802
It has published no outcome yet.

37
00:02:58,222 --> 00:03:06,100
Takeda's version: a governed data and decision layer, where every experiment and every go or no-go is logged against a baseline.

38
00:03:07,650 --> 00:03:09,481
Takeda already has the platform.

39
00:03:09,901 --> 00:03:13,168
Sixty-three percent of the workforce uses generative AI.

40
00:03:13,587 --> 00:03:15,578
But usage is adoption, not value.

41
00:03:15,998 --> 00:03:21,345
At Lessines, one hundred seventy predictive-maintenance agents run; their savings are unpublished.

42
00:03:21,765 --> 00:03:23,273
Baseline first, then claim.

43
00:03:23,693 --> 00:03:26,176
And whoever measures should not own the savings target.

44
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:29,937
In the laboratory, the same rule applies.

45
00:03:30,357 --> 00:03:35,819
Scripted automation, robots that dose, measure and screen, is mature and sold as a service.

46
00:03:36,239 --> 00:03:39,376
Remote cloud labs work but have proved commercially fragile.

47
00:03:39,796 --> 00:03:47,102
An AI that plans its own experiments is a prototype; first clinical data from such partnerships is still a year or two away.

48
00:03:47,522 --> 00:03:51,388
A fully autonomous discovery loop has not been demonstrated anywhere.

49
00:03:51,808 --> 00:03:57,917
So: rent automation, climb only when triggers fire, and gate the AI partners on first-in-human data.

50
00:03:59,483 --> 00:04:08,324
Pharmacy benefit managers now decide biosimilar outcomes: when CVS moved its templates to Stelara biosimilars, most members paid nothing.

51
00:04:08,744 --> 00:04:12,027
The Entyvio plan is honest: delay erosion, and measure it.

52
00:04:12,447 --> 00:04:17,911
The subcutaneous pen drives uptake and the HYHUB device brings plasma therapy home.

53
00:04:18,331 --> 00:04:21,289
But the pharmacy channel is also where biosimilars win.

54
00:04:21,709 --> 00:04:27,951
No company studied publishes adherence outcomes; Takeda can be the first, starting with the oveporexton launch.

55
00:04:29,517 --> 00:04:37,150
Takeda's instrument for partnerships is the mid-sized licence: Nimbus for four billion dollars upfront, Innovent for one point two.

56
00:04:37,570 --> 00:04:44,155
AbbVie runs early options worth up to a billion a year, yet none signed in this period has produced an approved product.

57
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:46,720
AbbVie wrote off half of Cerevel within months.

58
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:53,194
At two point six times leverage, with Amitiza pending, a five billion dollar purchase fails the arithmetic.

59
00:04:53,614 --> 00:04:57,077
Fund a licensing channel instead, released when leverage allows.

60
00:04:58,650 --> 00:04:59,843
And the platform dream?

61
00:05:00,263 --> 00:05:02,812
NVIDIA says CUDA made no money for ten years.

62
00:05:03,233 --> 00:05:06,629
SpaceX built Falcon nine for a fraction of NASA's estimate.

63
00:05:07,049 --> 00:05:11,667
Alphabet's other bets lost seven and a half billion dollars in twenty twenty-five alone.

64
00:05:12,087 --> 00:05:17,050
Regeneron's discovery platform did not stop its lead product falling forty-two percent.

65
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:20,771
Platforms compound slowly and protect no single product.

66
00:05:21,191 --> 00:05:29,657
So Takeda's long bets are capped options with stop rules, and the strengths it compounds are its own: plasma process data, and orexin biology.

67
00:05:31,217 --> 00:05:31,993
The sequence.

68
00:05:32,413 --> 00:05:38,997
Twenty twenty-seven: baselines, the data standard, rented automation and the Entyvio channel decision, together.

69
00:05:39,418 --> 00:05:47,176
Twenty twenty-eight: the Medicare price lands, the biosimilar playbook goes live, the AI partnerships face a go or no-go on data.

70
00:05:47,596 --> 00:05:59,004
The balanced envelope is about one point nine billion dollars over fourteen years, roughly three percent of today's R and D, plus a contingent pool for licences: planning assumptions, not a budget.

71
00:05:59,424 --> 00:06:05,422
The council that challenged this plan found no funded bet robust to severe pricing pressure; hence the gates.

72
00:06:06,983 --> 00:06:09,250
No single drug secures the next decade.

73
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:10,669
No acquisition.

74
00:06:11,089 --> 00:06:12,007
No technology.

75
00:06:12,427 --> 00:06:20,844
What endures is an organisation that discovers repeatedly, measures honestly, connects evidence to patients, and learns faster than the market moves.

76
00:06:21,264 --> 00:06:29,497
Takeda has the raw material: a franchise to defend, launches in hand, plasma and orexin to compound, and the discipline to stop.

77
00:06:29,917 --> 00:06:31,232
Build the system around them.

78
00:06:31,652 --> 00:06:33,152
Start in twenty twenty-seven.

79
00:06:33,572 --> 00:06:34,732
Measure from day one.

80
00:06:35,152 --> 00:06:36,440
Decide at every gate.
